"
Whether the critiques computed in this process are for an agent, which MCP's own rules answer and nobody else's.

method_compile and critique_run set it while they critique. Calypso, Iceberg and the critique browser critique in processes of their own, where it is false, so MCP's rules say nothing to a person. Everything else Renraku decides as for any rule: whether the rule is on, and the false positives and forced rules a manifest declares.
"
Class {
	#name : 'MCPAgentCritiquing',
	#superclass : 'DynamicVariable',
	#category : 'MCP-IDE-Critiques',
	#package : 'MCP-IDE',
	#tag : 'Critiques'
}

{ #category : 'accessing' }
MCPAgentCritiquing >> default [

	^ false
]
